claim:
For the zero-field ferromagnetic XYZ dimer with \(z\)-directed Dzyaloshinskii--Moriya coupling analyzed by Gürkan and Pashaev, assume \(J_z<J_y<J_x<0\), \(D\ge0\), \(T>0\), and set \[A= rac{J_x-J_y}{2}>0,\qquad P=- rac{J_x+J_y}{2}>0,\qquad Z=-J_z>0,\]\[
u(D)=\sqrt{P^2+D^2},\qquad 
u_c=A+Z,\qquad D_c=\sqrt{
u_c^2-P^2}.\]Define \[u_+(T)=T\,\operatorname{arsinh}\!\left(e^{Z/T}\cosh(A/T)ight),\qquad D_+(T)=\sqrt{u_+(T)^2-P^2},\]and define \(D_-(T)=0\) if \(e^{Z/T}\sinh(A/T)\le\cosh(P/T)\); otherwise set \[u_-(T)=T\,\operatorname{arcosh}\!\left(e^{Z/T}\sinh(A/T)ight),\qquad D_-(T)=\sqrt{u_-(T)^2-P^2}.\]Then the source concurrence is zero exactly for \[D_-(T)\le D\le D_+(T),\]and positive exactly outside that interval. Whenever \(D_-(T)>0\), \[D_-(T)<D_c<D_+(T).\]As \(T\downarrow0\), \[D_c-D_-(T)\sim rac{
u_c}{D_c}\,T e^{-2A/T},\qquad D_+(T)-D_c\sim rac{
u_c}{D_c}\,T e^{-2A/T},\]so the finite-temperature zero-concurrence interval born from the single \(T=0\) critical point has width \[D_+(T)-D_-(T)\sim rac{2
u_c}{D_c}\,T e^{-2A/T}.\]Thus the thermal broadening of the DM-driven entanglement transition is exponentially narrow at low temperature and asymptotically symmetric in \(D\) to leading order.
